ame{cos}⁡(2x)$ on $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ].$ Select the correct options below.\n$\\,$\nThe function $f(x)$ is\n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$\nConsequently, the {{field-2}}\nin the corresponding Fourier series of $f(x)$ must be zero." :question/worked-solution "To check whether $f$ is even or odd, we compare $f(-x)$ and $f(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-x) & =(-x)^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(-x)) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-2x) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x) \\\\  & =f(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $f(-x)=f(x),$ we have that $f$ is even.\n\nFor the Fourier series on $[-\\pi ,\\pi ],$ the sine coefficients are given by\n\n$$\n{b}_{n}=\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nHere, $f(x)$ is even and $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)$ is odd, so $f(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)$ is odd.\n\nNow, the integral of an odd function over $[-\\pi ,\\pi ]$ is $0.$ Thus, ${b}_{n}=0$ for all $n\\ge 1.$\n\nTherefore, the function $f(x)$ is $\\text{even}$ and the $\\text{sine terms}$ in its Fourier series must be zero."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186397481 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229175 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "532a73e6-e026-57c9-9bad-57cd2f75b6df" :knowledge-point/title "Parity Recognition and Series Type"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d6fb8e02-c2ed-54c2-a769-c0f5e618e887" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "even" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397483} {:answer/id #uuid "82f2576e-7f7d-514c-b7d3-b07f1e9d3631" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "odd" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397484}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "82f2576e-7f7d-514c-b7d3-b07f1e9d3631" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "odd" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397484} :answer-field/id #uuid "35a58589-56cd-5637-b523-03f859fac5b6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397482} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34d21a9d-340e-5cb4-a005-7da885a8f606" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "sine terms" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397486} {:answer/id #uuid "1b091b7e-9971-5f89-be72-b0882bfa2d62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "cosine terms" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397487}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1b091b7e-9971-5f89-be72-b0882bfa2d62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "cosine terms" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397487} :answer-field/id #uuid "52a06cf5-506a-5aec-8bcd-ea5d4fda8897" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397485}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8afd30f6-9418-5f9f-a8dd-bdb05d34a03e" :question/math-academy-id "q-340806" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x)={x}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)$ on $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ].$ Select the correct options below.\n\n$\\,$\nThe function $f(x)$ is\n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$\nConsequently, the \n{{field-2}}\nin the corresponding Fourier series of $f(x)$ must be zero." :question/worked-solution "To determine whether $f$ is even or odd, we compare $f(-x)$ and $f(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-x) & =(-x)^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-x) \\\\  & =-{x}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x) \\\\  & =-f(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $f(-x)=-f(x),$ we have that $f$ is odd.\n\nFor Fourier series on $[-\\pi ,\\pi ],$ the cosine coefficients are given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nand the constant coefficient is\n\n$$\n{a}_{0}=\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nHere, $f(x)$ is odd and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)$ is even, so $f(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)$ is odd. Also, $f(x)$ itself is odd.\n\nNow, the integral of an odd function over $[-\\pi ,\\pi ]$ is $0.$ Thus, ${a}_{n}=0$ for all $n\\ge 1,$ and ${a}_{0}=0.$\n\nTherefore, the function $f(x)$ is $\\text{odd}$ and the $\\text{cosine terms}$ in its Fourier series must be zero."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186511555 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229175 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "532a73e6-e026-57c9-9bad-57cd2f75b6df" :knowledge-point/title "Parity Recognition and Series Type"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "72a0583c-ea43-573f-b06b-b4a00d3b2c56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "even" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511020} {:answer/id #uuid "f5668d0f-beb2-5460-abcc-92d140689ec1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "odd" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511290}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f5668d0f-beb2-5460-abcc-92d140689ec1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "odd" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511290} :answer-field/id #uuid "19bcbcdc-3036-501a-8695-55f2eed0f886" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511325} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8459b090-9382-5cc1-a414-5ca52e5a7ae5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "cosine terms" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511053} {:answer/id #uuid "d9aad8a1-e2f8-56c6-bcac-8497da0fc04a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "sine terms" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511229}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8459b090-9382-5cc1-a414-5ca52e5a7ae5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.ty